From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 05:19:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: macaudio: Add the J604 jack

The J604 ADT places the jack codec exactly where the J713 one is: a
CS42L84 at 0x4b on i2c1, reset on nub GPIO 17, interrupt on AP GPIO 98,
fed by the AOP from admac-base-ns channels 4 (out) and 5 (in). Use the
J616s jack configuration as the J713 does, including its -6 dB cap on
the headphone DAC: this board's analog full scale is unmeasured too.

The speakers (six SN012776 on i2c3, 2W+1T per side) get no entry until
they have a bring-up of their own.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index 1a7519c2ea..2355fb3257 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -2247,6 +2247,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	/* j575    AID33   sn012776    15      1x 1W    Compat: apple,j375-macaudio */
 	/* j613    AID20   sn012776    15      2x 1W+1T Compat: apple,j413-macaudio */
 	/* j615    AID21   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T Compat: apple,j415-macaudio */
+	/* j604    AID30   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j604-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j614    AID34   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed; speakers off until bring-up) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j614-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j614_cfg },
 	/* j614    AID34   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
